From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: one-step CPU OPP voltages

Diagnostic only, not for merging. Run every CPU OPP below 1.8 GHz one 6.25 mV step under the 1.8 GHz voltage
so that every frequency change still writes the regulator over i2c0 but the
electrical step is negligible. If the resets
under software-ISP load stop, they are caused by the size of the voltage step;
if they continue, by the transaction itself.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic experiment]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN op_a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi op_b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-19 06:23:36.494639300 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-19 06:23:36.516164368 +0200
@@ -281,6 +281,28 @@
 	cpu-supply = <&vdd_cpu>;
 };
 
+/* EXPERIMENT: writes without a real step - see the patch description. */
+&cpu0_opp_table {
+	opp-408000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1143750 1143750 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-600000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1143750 1143750 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-816000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1143750 1143750 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1104000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1143750 1143750 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1416000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1143750 1143750 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1608000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1143750 1143750 1150000>;
+	};
+};
+
 &cru {
 	assigned-clocks = <&pmucru CLK_RTC_32K>, <&cru PLL_GPLL>,
 			  <&pmucru PLL_PPLL>, <&cru PLL_VPLL>;
